🚀 Day 19 of #DrGViswanathanChallenge

Today, I solved LeetCode 283 – Move Zeroes.

This problem is another great application of the Two Pointers technique. The goal was to move all 0s to the end while maintaining the relative order of non-zero elements, all in-place with O(1) extra space.

💡 Approach: Two Pointers + In-Place Swapping

I used two pointers:

i → Traverses the entire array.
j → Tracks the position where the next non-zero element should be placed.

Whenever a non-zero element is found, I swap it with the element at pointer j and increment j. This keeps all non-zero elements at the front while naturally pushing zeroes toward the end.

⏱️ Time Complexity: O(n)
💾 Space Complexity: O(1)

